{
  "text": " They were big. Everybody from the tarn was big, as if the hills grew them on purpose. Their captain was a thin dark girl with a still door, who walked as though the stone under her were a field she knew. The others came behind her, a heavy blade, a hold with long arms, a catcher with a fresh bandage on one wrist. They stood behind their hurdle and looked down the pen at seven, and Kaiva saw them look at the linen on her right hand, and Prue's ten caps, and Jude's left arm hanging, and Perrin standing outside the pen with his hand pressed to his side.",
